# Dev Notes 36 — Runtime Capability Bus Skeleton v1

**Date:** 2026-06-15  
**Branch:** `runtime-capability-bus-skeleton-v1`  
**Repo:** `Main-Michael-Sparks/runtime-dev-repo`  
**Status:** Staged in sandbox; syntax-checked and contract-smoke-tested locally in the assistant sandbox. Not GitHub-verified until Michael uploads/pushes the branch and provides a repo link.

---

## Purpose

Add the first non-executing Capability Bus skeleton contract around the existing Runtime Dev bus contracts.

This branch answers, in code and tests:

```text
how a bus intake helper validates an action envelope against a capability registry
how a bus intake helper confirms the requested capability exists in the registry
how deprecated capability definitions are rejected at bus intake
how bus-level result helpers return contract-valid failed / policy-denied skeleton outcomes
how bus-level event helpers return contract-valid accepted / failed / policy-denied skeleton events
how the bus skeleton stays modular and bus-local without runtime or worker execution wiring
```

This remains contract-only. It does not make any capability executable.

