## Modular design shape

The `runtime/bus/` namespace remains a contract namespace:

```text
contractValidation.mjs              shared validation result/error helpers and safe object checks
capabilityTaxonomy.mjs              frozen v1 capability/status/event/source-kind constants
capabilityDefinition.mjs            capability definition metadata contract
capabilityRegistryContract.mjs      registry validation, creation, lookup, and listing contract helpers
capabilityBusContract.mjs           non-executing bus intake validation against action + registry contracts
capabilityBusResult.mjs             bus-level skeleton result-envelope constructors
capabilityBusEvents.mjs             bus-level skeleton action-event constructors
contextRefs.mjs                     context reference validation and normalization
actionEnvelope.mjs                  action request contract validation/normalization
resultEnvelope.mjs                  normalized result/error contract validation/creation
actionEvent.mjs                     action event contract validation/creation
```

New bus skeleton modules import only existing `runtime/bus/**` contract helpers.

No `runtime.mjs`, `workerBridge.mjs`, `runtime/lifecycle/**`, `runtime/request/**`, `runtime/stream/**`, `runtime/observability/**`, or `llama_worker/**` imports were introduced.

---

## Contract behavior summary

### Capability Bus intake

`runtime/bus/capabilityBusContract.mjs` exports:

```text
CAPABILITY_BUS_CONTRACT_VERSION
normalizeCapabilityBusAction()
validateCapabilityBusAction()
assertCapabilityBusAction()
```

Normalized shape:

```js
const busAction = {
    contractVersion: "capability-bus.v1",
    action: normalizedActionEnvelope,
    capabilityDefinition: normalizedCapabilityDefinition
};
```

Validation behavior:

```text
validates the action envelope through actionEnvelope.mjs
validates the registry through capabilityRegistryContract.mjs
prefixes action validation paths/codes with action / bus_action
prefixes registry validation paths/codes with registry / bus_registry
rejects when the requested capability is not defined in the registry
rejects deprecated capability definitions at bus intake
returns a normalized non-executing wrapper when valid
```

This helper does not dispatch, route, enqueue, stream, call a backend, or touch worker/native code.

### Capability Bus result helpers

`runtime/bus/capabilityBusResult.mjs` exports:

```text
createCapabilityNotImplementedResult()
createCapabilityUnsupportedResult()
createCapabilityPolicyDeniedResult()
createCapabilityValidationFailedResult()
```

These helpers create contract-valid result envelopes using existing result-envelope semantics:

```text
not implemented      -> status: failed,        error.kind: runtime,    code: capability_not_implemented
unsupported          -> status: failed,        error.kind: validation, code: capability_unsupported
policy denied        -> status: policy_denied, error.kind: policy,     code: capability_policy_denied
validation failed    -> status: failed,        error.kind: validation, code: capability_bus_validation_failed
```

They copy only safe action identity fields from the action envelope:

```text
actionId
runId
capability
```

They do not include backend options, raw backend payloads, model paths, tool process fields, command fields, environment fields, or adapter args.

### Capability Bus event helpers

`runtime/bus/capabilityBusEvents.mjs` exports:

```text
createCapabilityBusAcceptedEvent()
createCapabilityBusRejectedEvent()
createCapabilityBusNotImplementedEvent()
createCapabilityBusPolicyDeniedEvent()
```

Event behavior:

```text
accepted             -> type: action.accepted
rejected             -> type: action.failed
not implemented      -> type: action.failed
policy denied        -> type: action.policyDenied
```

The helpers require caller-supplied `eventId` and `timestamp`. They do not call `Date.now()` and do not generate hidden event IDs. This keeps the skeleton contract deterministic and avoids introducing event-sink/runtime-time behavior in this branch.

